--
-- The Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238: what a repeal does (ss 4(4), 32,
-- 35, 36). The moments at which an enactment ceases to have effect (s 4(2), 4(3)) are in
-- `bc-interpretation-time.l4`.
--
-- Draft. A single Sonnet 5.5 agent wrote this from the text alone; no domain expert has read it
-- against the statute. The quotations are copied from `RSBC-1996-c.-238.txt`, a plain-text
-- rendering made by a script (not the official text), by `srcrefs.py`; `src:N` is line N of that file.
--
-- Target compiler: `unstable` (REFUSE and YMD are rejected by `main`).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `s 4(4) Expiry is repeal`

-- src:38 | (4) An enactment that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect is deemed to be repealed for the purposes of this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 4(4) (src:38)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(4) speaks only of an enactment that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 4(4) speaks only of an enactment that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect"

-- src:38 | (4) An enactment that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect is deemed to be repealed for the purposes of this Act.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 4(4) (src:38)
GIVEN `the enactment has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 4(4) the enactment is deemed to be repealed for the purposes of this Act` `the enactment has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect` MEANS
    IF   `the enactment has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect`
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE `s 4(4) speaks only of an enactment that has expired or otherwise ceased to have effect`

§ `s 32 References to enactments that are amended or repealed`

DECLARE `The enactment that a reference in an enactment of British Columbia names` IS ONE OF
    `A domestic enactment that has been amended, including by repeal and replacement on the same subject matter, revision or consolidation`
        HAS `the day of the subsequent transaction, matter or thing` IS A DATE
    `A domestic enactment that has been repealed and not replaced with a domestic enactment on the same subject matter`
        HAS `the last day on which the repealed enactment had effect` IS A DATE
    `A foreign enactment`
        HAS `the day the enactment of British Columbia containing the reference was enacted` IS A DATE

-- The answer is the day whose text of the named enactment the reference is to be read as
-- naming. For an amended domestic enactment it is the day of the subsequent transaction,
-- matter or thing (s 32(2)): the amended text, whenever the amendment was made (s 32(3)).
-- For one repealed and not replaced it is the last day on which it had effect, "as it read
-- immediately before its repeal" (s 32(4)); the caller finds that day with s 4(2) or s 4(3).
-- For a foreign enactment it is the day the referring enactment was enacted (s 32(5)).
-- src:365 | (a) the repeal and replacement of the domestic enactment with a domestic enactment in relation to the same subject matter, and
-- src:366 | (b) the revision or consolidation of the domestic enactment;
-- src:369 | (2) If a domestic enactment is amended, a reference in an unrepealed enactment of British Columbia to the domestic enactment is to be construed, for a subsequent transaction, matter or thing, as a reference to the amended domestic enactment.
-- src:370 | (3) Subsection (2) applies whether the domestic enactment is amended before, at the same time as or after the coming into force of the enactment of British Columbia in which the reference to the domestic enactment appears.
-- src:371 | (4) If a domestic enactment is repealed and not replaced with a domestic enactment in relation to the same subject matter, a reference in an unrepealed enactment of British Columbia to the domestic enactment is to be construed, for a subsequent transaction, matter or thing, as a reference to the repealed domestic enactment as it read immediately before its repeal.
-- src:372 | (5) A reference in an enactment of British Columbia to a foreign enactment is to be construed as a reference to the foreign enactment as it read on the date the enactment of British Columbia containing the reference to that foreign enactment was enacted.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 32(1), (2), (3), (4) and (5) (src:365-366, src:369-372)
GIVEN named IS A `The enactment that a reference in an enactment of British Columbia names`
GIVETH A DATE
`s 32 the day whose text of the named enactment the reference is to` named MEANS
    CONSIDER named
        WHEN `A domestic enactment that has been amended, including by repeal and replacement on the same subject matter, revision or consolidation` transactionDay THEN transactionDay
        WHEN `A domestic enactment that has been repealed and not replaced with a domestic enactment on the same subject matter` lastDay THEN lastDay
        WHEN `A foreign enactment` enactedOn THEN enactedOn

§ `s 35 Repeal`

DECLARE `Matter a repeal might touch` IS ONE OF
    `Reviving an enactment or thing not in force or existing immediately before the time when the repeal takes effect`
    `The previous operation of the repealed enactment, or anything done or suffered under it`
    `A right or obligation acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the repealed enactment`
    `An offence committed against, or a contravention of, the repealed enactment, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred under it`
    `An investigation, proceeding or remedy for such a right, obligation, penalty, forfeiture or punishment`

-- Para (d) is "subject to section 36 (1) (d)": a penalty, forfeiture or punishment that a
-- substituted enactment reduces or mitigates is reduced when it is imposed or adjusted after
-- the repeal. `reducedBySubstitute` is that condition.
-- src:386 | 35 (1) If all or part of an enactment is repealed, the repeal does not
-- src:387 | (a) revive an enactment or thing not in force or existing immediately before the time when the repeal takes effect,
-- src:388 | (b) affect the previous operation of the enactment so repealed or anything done or suffered under it,
-- src:389 | (c) affect a right or obligation acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the enactment so repealed,
-- src:390 | (d) subject to section 36 (1) (d), affect an offence committed against or a contravention of the repealed enactment, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred under it, or
-- src:391 | (e) affect an investigation, proceeding or remedy for the right, obligation, penalty, forfeiture or punishment.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 35(1) (src:386-391)
GIVEN matter             IS A `Matter a repeal might touch`
      reducedBySubstitute IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 35(1) the repeal leaves the matter unaffected` matter reducedBySubstitute MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
        WHEN `Reviving an enactment or thing not in force or existing immediately before the time when the repeal takes effect` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `The previous operation of the repealed enactment, or anything done or suffered under it` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A right or obligation acquired, accrued, accruing or incurred under the repealed enactment` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `An offence committed against, or a contravention of, the repealed enactment, or a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred under it` THEN NOT reducedBySubstitute
        WHEN `An investigation, proceeding or remedy for such a right, obligation, penalty, forfeiture or punishment` THEN TRUE

DECLARE `Basis on which an investigation, proceeding or remedy goes on after a repeal` IS ONE OF
    `As if the enactment had not been repealed`
    `As if the enactment had not been repealed, subject to section 36 (1) because another enactment is substituted`

-- src:392 | (2) Subject to section 36 (1), an investigation, proceeding or remedy described in subsection (1) (e) may be instituted, continued or enforced and the penalty, forfeiture or punishment imposed as if the enactment had not been repealed.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 35(2) (src:392)
GIVEN anotherEnactmentIsSubstituted IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Basis on which an investigation, proceeding or remedy goes on after a repeal`
`s 35(2) the basis on which an investigation, proceeding or remedy may be instituted, continued or enforced` anotherEnactmentIsSubstituted MEANS
    IF   anotherEnactmentIsSubstituted
    THEN `As if the enactment had not been repealed, subject to section 36 (1) because another enactment is substituted`
    ELSE `As if the enactment had not been repealed`

§ `s 36 Repeal and replacement`

-- src:395 | 36 (1) If an enactment (the "former enactment") is repealed and another enactment (the "new enactment") is substituted for it,
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 36(1) (src:395)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 36(1) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one"

-- src:396 | (a) every person acting under the former enactment must continue to act as if appointed or elected under the new enactment until another is appointed or elected in the person's place,
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 36(1)(a) (src:396)
GIVEN anotherEnactmentIsSubstituted IS A BOOLEAN
      anotherIsAppointedOrElectedInThePersonsPlace IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1)(a) a person acting under the former enactment must continue to act` anotherEnactmentIsSubstituted anotherIsAppointedOrElectedInThePersonsPlace MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT anotherEnactmentIsSubstituted THEN `s 36(1) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one`
        OTHERWISE NOT anotherIsAppointedOrElectedInThePersonsPlace

-- "reduced or mitigated": the caller supplies the figure under each enactment (for example the
-- maximum fine). A forfeiture or a punishment that is not a number is not covered by this function.
-- src:399 | (d) when a penalty, forfeiture or punishment is reduced or mitigated by the new enactment, the penalty, forfeiture or punishment if imposed or adjusted after the repeal must be reduced or mitigated accordingly, and
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 36(1)(d) (src:399)
GIVEN `the penalty under the former enactment` IS A NUMBER
      `the penalty under the new enactment`    IS A NUMBER
      `it is imposed or adjusted after the repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 36(1)(d) the penalty that may be imposed or adjusted` `the penalty under the former enactment` `the penalty under the new enactment` `it is imposed or adjusted after the repeal` MEANS
    IF   `it is imposed or adjusted after the repeal` AND `the penalty under the new enactment` BELOW `the penalty under the former enactment`
    THEN `the penalty under the new enactment`
    ELSE `the penalty under the former enactment`

-- "insofar as they are not inconsistent with the new enactment, until they are repealed or others
-- are made in their place": the caller says whether the regulation (or the part asked about)
-- is inconsistent, repealed, or replaced.
-- src:400 | (e) all regulations made under the former enactment remain in force and are deemed to have been made under the new enactment, insofar as they are not inconsistent with the new enactment, until they are repealed or others are made in their place.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 36(1)(e) (src:400)
GIVEN anotherEnactmentIsSubstituted IS A BOOLEAN
      inconsistentWithTheNewEnactment IS A BOOLEAN
      hasBeenRepealed                 IS A BOOLEAN
      othersHaveBeenMadeInItsPlace    IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 36(1)(e) a regulation made under the former enactment remains in force` anotherEnactmentIsSubstituted inconsistentWithTheNewEnactment hasBeenRepealed othersHaveBeenMadeInItsPlace MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT anotherEnactmentIsSubstituted THEN `s 36(1) applies only where another enactment is substituted for the repealed one`
        OTHERWISE
                NOT inconsistentWithTheNewEnactment
            AND NOT hasBeenRepealed
            AND NOT othersHaveBeenMadeInItsPlace
